         </draw:image>
        </draw:frame>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure1" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">2.2</text:sequence>: Ubuntu Live CD Initial Display.</text:p>
      </draw:text-box>
     </draw:frame><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
    <text:list xml:id="list140623270029799" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="_40_BulletList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P681">Select the “Install Ubuntu” option to install the operating system. The “Try Ubuntu” option means the guest machine will run from a “Live CD”.</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P682">F<text:span text:style-name="T6">ollow the on screen instructions to install the operating system, </text:span>together with any updates suggested by the installer. Once the installation is complete the guest machine will re-boot as a normal guest Linux machine.</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:list xml:id="list140623243759516" text:continue-list="list140624598828600" text:style-name="_40_NumberList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:list>
         <text:list-item>
          <text:p text:style-name="P673">Installing OPM Flow in the Guest Virtual Machine.</text:p>
         </text:list-item>
        </text:list>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:list text:continue-list="list140623270029799" text:style-name="_40_BulletList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P667">Boot up your virtual machine by selecting the machine and selecting the “Start” icon on the main VirtualBox screen (<text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refFigure0">Figure 2.1</text:sequence-ref>). One should then be presented with the newly created guest virtual machine, similar to one shown in <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refFigure2">Figure 2.3</text:sequence-ref>, that displays the standard Ubuntu desktop.</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P668"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr19" draw:name="Frame56" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="4.591cm" svg:y="-0.178cm" svg:width="10.947cm" draw:z-index="4">
          <draw:text-box fo:min-height="9.618cm">
           <text:p text:style-name="Figure"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr27" draw:name="Image50" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="10.663cm" style:rel-width="100%" svg:height="9.043cm" style:rel-height="scale" draw:z-index="5"><draw:image draw:mime-type="image/png">
