         </draw:image>
        </draw:frame>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure5" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">2.6</text:sequence>: Windows 10 - Activate WSL</text:p>
      </draw:text-box>
     </draw:frame>You may also have to <text:span text:style-name="T40">ensure that CPU virtualization. </text:span>has been activated in your computer’s BIOS.</text:p>
    <text:list xml:id="list140623522986271" text:continue-list="list140624326493038" text:style-name="_40_NumberList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:list>
         <text:list-item>
          <text:p text:style-name="P674">Installing a Linux Distribution.</text:p>
         </text:list-item>
        </text:list>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:list text:continue-list="list140624156402530" text:style-name="_40_BulletList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P675">To install the Linux
	distribution in Windows, click Start and then select the Microsoft Store.</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P675">Using the search box available in the Microsoft Store, pick one of the distributions that is compatible with OPM Flow (<text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refFigure6">Figure 2.7</text:sequence-ref>). Note that for Ubuntu these are usually the two latest LTS versions before the release, i.e. version &quot;20XX.04 LTS&quot; where XX is a multiple of 4.</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:p text:style-name="P79"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr2" draw:name="Frame59" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="3.362cm" svg:y="0cm" svg:width="12.809cm" draw:z-index="12">
      <draw:text-box fo:min-height="5.53cm">
