      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P670">When starting the Linux Distribution for the first time, a brief setup process will take place. Basically, it will ask for the username and password you want to set for the Linux environment, a similar process as when you install a Linux distribution via VirtualBox.</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P676">To check the version of WSL that will be used to run the Linux distribution, in PowerShell use the following command:</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:p text:style-name="P136">wsl -l -v</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P596"/>
    <text:list text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="_40_BulletList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P683">To set the WSL for a given distribution, for example Ubuntu-24-04 to WSL 2, in PowerShell use the following command:</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:p text:style-name="P135">wsl --set-version Ubuntu-24-04 2</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:list xml:id="list140623648888723" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="_40_BulletList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P664">And finally to set the default version for WSL for all Linux distributions, use the following PowerShell command:</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:p text:style-name="P136">wsl --set-default-version 2</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P263"/>
    <text:list xml:id="list140624075405992" text:continue-list="list140623522986271" text:style-name="_40_NumberList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:list>
         <text:list-item>
          <text:p text:style-name="P684">Installing OPM Flow in a WSL Linux Distribution:</text:p>
         </text:list-item>
        </text:list>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:list xml:id="list140624923639235" text:continue-list="list140623648888723" text:style-name="_40_BulletList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P685">Click on installed Linux distribution in the Start Menu to open a Linux terminal session, and then execute the Linux commands as described earlier in Sections <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#2.1.1.Ubuntu Linux 24.04 (64-bit version only) and Higher|outline" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="number" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc121657_2412586160">2.1.1</text:bookmark-ref><text:s/><text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="text" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc121657_2412586160">Ubuntu Linux 22.04 or 24.04 (64-bit version only)</text:bookmark-ref></text:a><text:s/>and <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#2.1.2.Red Hat Enterprise or CentOS (version 7 or 8)|outline" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="number" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc121659_2412586160">2.1.2</text:bookmark-ref><text:s/><text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="text" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc121659_2412586160">Red Hat Enterprise or CentOS (version 7 or 8)</text:bookmark-ref></text:a><text:s/>to install the software. <text:s/></text:p>
       </text:list-item>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P686"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T6">To check if OPM Flow is installed, execute the following command in the </text:span>Linux <text:span text:style-name="T6">terminal window:</text:span></text:p>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:p text:style-name="P139">f<text:span text:style-name="T6">low –-help</text:span></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P106"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="P572">which should then display the command line parameters for the installed version of OPM Flow, as depicted in <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refFigure8">Figure 2.9</text:sequence-ref>.</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P270"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr2" draw:name="Frame62" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="3.136cm" svg:y="0cm" svg:width="13.869cm" draw:z-index="16">
