          </office:binary-data>
         </draw:image>
        </draw:frame>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure8" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">2.9</text:sequence>: Windows 10 WSL - Running OPM Flow Help</text:p>
      </draw:text-box>
     </draw:frame></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P569">One can also use the Windows command terminal, instead of the WSL Linux Terminal, to do the same thing by adding WSL character string before the command, that is:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P140">wsl f<text:span text:style-name="T6">low –-help</text:span></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P112"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="P570"/>
    <text:list xml:id="list140624426192751" text:continue-list="list140624075405992" text:style-name="_40_NumberList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:list>
         <text:list-item>
          <text:p text:style-name="P658">Using OPM Flow via the Windows <text:s/>WSL Linux Virtual Machine.</text:p>
         </text:list-item>
        </text:list>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:list text:continue-list="list140624923639235" text:style-name="_40_BulletList">
     <text:list-item>
      <text:list>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P671">Similar to running OPM Flow using a Linux distribution installed in VirtualBox, the WSL Linux virtual machine only has access to files within WSL virtual machine. <text:s/>To access the Windows file system, one has to execute the Linux CD command in the WSL Linux Terminal, the command has the form:</text:p>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
     </text:list-item>
    </text:list>
    <text:p text:style-name="P37">cd /mnt/&lt;drive letter&gt;</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P438"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="P307">For example, to access the Windows system drive C one would use the following command:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P138">cd /mnt/c</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="P306">One can then run OPM Flow from the desired directory in the WSL Linux virtual machine and use OPM ResInsight under Windows  to view the results of the simulation run.</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P456">User experience indicates this approach of running OPM Flow under Windows is the most integrated and convenient method, compared to the VirtualBox approach, especially for the less technically advance users.</text:p>
    <text:h text:style-name="P120" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc439882_869316532"/><text:soft-page-break/>Using a Docker Container<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc439882_869316532"/></text:h>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">See the tutorial on the OPM website<text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"> </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="http://opm-project.org/?page_id=853&amp;page=2" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">Running Flow in Docker</text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link">.</text:span></text:p>
    <text:h text:style-name="P121" text:outline-level="3"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc105053_3650259404"/>Installing from Source<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc105053_3650259404"/></text:h>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"><text:span text:style-name="T6">See instructions on the OPM website </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="http://opm-project.org/?page_id=231" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">Building from Source</text:a>.</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"><text:span text:style-name="Internet_20_link"/></text:p>
    <text:h text:style-name="P117" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__RefHeading___Toc144424_3025544877"/>Running OPM Flow From The Command Line<text:bookmark-end text:name="__RefHeading___Toc144424_3025544877"/></text:h>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">This section describes how to run the OPM Flow simulator and the various command line options associated with this release, the command line syntax for running OPM Flow is:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:tab/><text:tab/>flow [OPTIONS] CASENAME </text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">and typing the following command from your terminal:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:tab/><text:tab/>flow CASENAME</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">will start the simulator and run the case specified by CASENAME.DATA. <text:s/>Alternatively, you can type the path to the binary and the *.DATA file, as per the example below:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:tab/><text:tab/>path_to_binary/flow path_to_data/CASENAME </text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">The simulator can also be run using command line parameters for example to run the previous CASENAME one could use:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:tab/><text:tab/>flow --ecl-deck-file-name=path_to_data/CASENAME </text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">Note that there must be no spaces around the equals sign and there should be no spaces in CASENAME. If there are spaces in CASENAME, which can typically occur on Windows based systems, then the CASENAME should be enclosed in quotes; thus instead of CASE NAME use “CASE NAME”.</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">By default output files are generated in the same folder as the *.DATA file. <text:s/>To override this one can use the --output-dir command line parameter, for instance:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:tab/><text:tab/>flow --output-dir=foo CASENAME </text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">will send the output files to the foo directory. <text:s text:c="2"/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">It is also possible to put multiple command line options together in a parameter file. To do so, put one option on each line of the file with “.param” as the extension and pass that filename as a command line parameter to OPM Flow using:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:tab/><text:tab/>flow --parameter-file=CASENAME.param</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">to instruct OPM Flow to read the parameter file. Note, it is good practice to name both the *.DATA and parameter file with the same CASENAME, to avoid confusion. However, if one wishes to use the same parameter file for various cases one can specify the parameter file followed by the DATA file, for example:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:tab/><text:tab/>flow --parameter-file=path_to_params/ALLCASES.param CASENAME.DATA</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">Frequently used command line options to be used for all runs can be added to a configuration file in the user's home directory:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:tab/><text:tab/>$(HOME)/.config/OpmFlow/user_parameters.param</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">The file format is the same as for a standard parameter file. Parameters specified on the command line or via the --parameter-file will take precedence.</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">If OPM Flow is installed with parallel capabilities then:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:tab/><text:tab/>mpirun -np 4 flow --parameter-file=path_to_data/CASENAME.param </text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">will run OPM Flow on four nodes etc. </text:p>
    <table:table table:name="Table758" table:style-name="Table758">
     <table:table-column table:style-name="Table758.A"/>
     <table:table-header-rows>
      <table:table-row>
       <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table758.A1" office:value-type="string">
        <text:p text:style-name="P48">Note</text:p>
        <text:p text:style-name="P60">On Red Hat based distributions, including centOS distributions, one needs to install the openmpi version of the simulator, opm-simulators-openmpi-bin, via:</text:p>
        <text:p text:style-name="P59">sudo yum install opm-simulators-openmpi-bin</text:p>
        <text:p text:style-name="P60">and then set the MPI version to use. The way this is done is by first making the module command available, by running the following command:</text:p>
        <text:p text:style-name="P59">. /usr/share/Modules/init/bash</text:p>
        <text:p text:style-name="P60">Then query for the installed modules with:</text:p>
        <text:p text:style-name="P59">module avail</text:p>
        <text:p text:style-name="P60">And lastly, you tell the system it to use openmpi with:</text:p>
        <text:p text:style-name="P59">module add mpi/openmpi-x86_64</text:p>
        <text:p text:style-name="P60">On Ubuntu based distributions, there is no need for this as openmpi is installed and mpirun just works.</text:p>
       </table:table-cell>
      </table:table-row>
     </table:table-header-rows>
    </table:table>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">A complete list of the active user facing command line options and their function is given in <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refTable0">Table 2.1</text:sequence-ref><text:s/>for the current release. These commands are the options listed with command line --help option, there is also a --help-all option that lists all the command line options included in the release, including experimental, obsolete, hidden and deprecated options. </text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="_40_TextBody">Additional tutorials for running OPM Flow are available on the OPM website in the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="http://opm-project.org/?page_id=43" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">Tutorials</text:a> section.</text:p>
    <table:table table:name="Table621" table:style-name="Table621">
     <table:table-column table:style-name="Table621.A"/>
     <table:table-column table:style-name="Table621.B"/>
     <table:table-column table:style-name="Table621.C"/>
     <table:table-column table:style-name="Table621.D"/>
     <table:table-header-rows>
      <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.1">
       <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A1" table:number-columns-spanned="4" office:value-type="string">
        <text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">OPM Flow Command Line Options</text:p>
       </table:table-cell>
       <table:covered-table-cell/>
       <table:covered-table-cell/>
       <table:covered-table-cell/>
      </table:table-row>
      <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
       <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
        <text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">No.</text:p>
       </table:table-cell>
       <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
        <text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">Variable Name</text:p>
       </table:table-cell>
       <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
        <text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">Description</text:p>
       </table:table-cell>
       <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
        <text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">Default</text:p>
       </table:table-cell>
      </table:table-row>
     </table:table-header-rows>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">-h or --help</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Print the help message that gives a brief description of the available command line parameters.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">N/A</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A3&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="2">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">2</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--help-all</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Prints all the command line options included in the release, including obsolete, hidden and deprecated options.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">N/A</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A4&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="3">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">3</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--accelerator-mode</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Choose a linear solver. Valid options are: cusparse, opencl, amgcl, rocalution, rocsparse, and none. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;none&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A5&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="4">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">4</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--action-parsing-strictness</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Set strictness of parsing process for ActionX and PyAction. Available options are normal (do not apply keywords that have not been tested for ActionX or PyAction) and low (try to apply all keywords, beware: the simulation outcome might be incorrect). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;normal&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A6&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="5">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">5</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--add-corners</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Add corners to partition. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A7&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="6">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">6</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--allow-distributed-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Allow the perforations of a well to be distributed to interior of multiple processes. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A8&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="7">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">7</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--allow-splitting-inactive-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Allow inactive (never non-shut) wells to be split across multiple domains. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A9&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="8">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">8</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--alternative-well-rate-init</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Use alternative well rate initialization procedure. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A10&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="9">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">9</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--check-group-constraints-inner-well-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Allow checking of group constraints during inner well iterations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A11&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="10">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">10</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--check-satfunc-consistency</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Whether or not to check saturation function consistency requirements. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A12&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="11">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">11</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--conserve-inner-energy-thermal</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Conserve inner energy and not enthalpy even if <text:a xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc137276_650382403">THERMAL</text:a> is used. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A13&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="12">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">12</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--continue-on-convergence-error</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Continue with a non-converged solution instead of giving up if we encounter a time step size smaller than the minimum time step size. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A14&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="13">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">13</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--convergence-monitoring</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Enable convergence monitoring. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A15&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="14">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">14</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--convergence-monitoring-cut-off</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Cut off limit for convergence monitoring. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">6</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A16&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="15">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">15</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--convergence-monitoring-decay-factor</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Decay factor for convergence monitoring. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.75</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A4">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">16</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.B2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--convert-to-multisegment-well</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.C2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Convert plain single-segment wells into multisegment wells so the wellbore hydrostatic head is handled implicitly. Valid options are: 'none' (default) or 'per-connection' (one linear tubing, a segment per connection). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">"none"</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A18&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="17">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">17</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--cpr-reuse-interval</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Reuse preconditioner interval. Used when CprReuseSetup is set to 4, then the preconditioner will be fully recreated instead of reused every N linear solves, where N is this parameter. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">30</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A19&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="18">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">18</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--cpr-reuse-setup</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive integer. Specify if the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc27871_3671211675" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">CPR</text:a> solver should re-use the AMG setup. Valid options are:</text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberOptions_3a_Table">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="0">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Recreate the preconditioner for every linear solve,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Recreate once every time step,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Recreate if last linear solve took more than 10 iterations,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Never recreate, or</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Recreate every N linear solves, where N is the parameter defined by <text:span text:style-name="T61">--cpr-reuse-interval</text:span>.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">4</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A20&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="19">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">19</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--cpr-weights-thread-parallel</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Enable OpenMP thread parallelization of <text:a xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc27871_3671211675">CPR</text:a> weight calculation. This can improve performance for large models but is disabled by default. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A21&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="20">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">20</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--dbhp-max-rel</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum relative change of the bottom-hole pressure in a single iteration. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A22&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="21">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">21</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--debug-emit-cell-partition</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Whether or not to emit cell partitions as a debugging aid. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A23&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="22">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">22</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--debug-verbosity-level</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Set debug verbosity level globally. Default is 1, increasing values give additional output and 0 disables most messages to the .DBG file. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A24&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="23">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">23</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--dp-max-rel</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum relative change of pressure in a single iteration. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.3</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A25&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="24">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">24</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--ds-max</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum absolute change of any saturation in a single iteration. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.2</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A26&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="25">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">25</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--dwell-fraction-max</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum absolute change of a well&apos;s volume fraction in a single iteration. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.2</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A27&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="26">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">26</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--ecl-deck-file-name</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. The name of the file which contains the ECL deck to be simulated. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A28&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="27">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">27</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--ecl-output-double-precision</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Tell the output writer to use double precision. Useful for &apos;perfect&apos; restarts. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A29&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="28">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">28</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--ecl-output-interval</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The number of report steps that ought to be skipped between two writes of ECL results. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">-1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A30&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="29">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">29</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--edge-conformal</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Edge conformal cornerpoint processing. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A31&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="30">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">30</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--edge-weights-method</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A defined character string. Specify the edge-weighting strategy:</text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;uniform&quot;,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;transmissibility&quot;, or</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;logtrans&quot; for the logarithm of transmissibility.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;transmissibility&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A32&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="31">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">31</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-adaptive-time-stepping</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Use adaptive time stepping between report steps. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A33&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="32">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">32</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-async-ecl-output</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Write the ECL-formated results in a non-blocking way (i.e., using a separate thread). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A34&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="33">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">33</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-async-vtk-output</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Dispatch a separate thread to write the VTK output. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A35&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="34">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">34</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-drift-compensation</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Enable partial compensation of systematic mass losses via the source term of the next time step. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A36&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="35">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">35</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-drift-compensation-temp</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Enable compensation of systematic mass losses in the energy equation (only <text:a xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc146397_3544483072">TEMP</text:a> option). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A37&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="36">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">36</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-dry-run</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A string value. Specify if the simulation should actually run (true), or just check the input deck (false).</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">This option is equivalent to activating the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc251745_4250154414" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">NOSIM</text:a> keyword in the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc55591_1778172979" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">RUNSPEC</text:a> section of the input deck.</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">The default value of &quot;auto&quot; will use whatever is stipulated in the input deck via the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc251745_4250154414" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">NOSIM</text:a> keyword. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;auto&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A38&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="37">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">37</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-ecl-output</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Write binary output which is compatible with the commercial Eclipse simulator. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A39&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="38">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">38</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-esmry</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Write ESMRY file for fast loading of summary data. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A40&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="39">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">39</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-gravity</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Use the gravity correction for the pressure gradients. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A41&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="40">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">40</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-grid-adaptation</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Enable adaptive grid refinement/coarsening. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A42&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="41">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">41</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-intensive-quantity-cache</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Turn on caching of intensive quantities. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A43&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="42">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">42</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-logging-fallout-warning</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Developer option to see whether logging was on non-root processors. In that case it will be appended to the *.DBG or *.PRT files. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A44&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="43">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">43</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-opm-rst-file</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Include OPM-specific keywords in the ECL restart file to enable restart of OPM simulators from these files. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A4" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A45&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="44">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">44</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.B2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-state-rollback</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.C2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Enable in-memory state snapshotting and restoration on unconverged Newton iterations and chopped time steps. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A46&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="45">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">45</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-storage-cache</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Store previous storage terms and avoid re-calculating them. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A47&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="46">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">46</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-terminal-output</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Print high-level information about the simulation&apos;s progress to the terminal. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A48&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="47">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">47</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-thermodynamic-hints</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Enable thermodynamic hints. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A49&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="48">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">48</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-tuning</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Read the time stepping and convergence parameters from the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc146744_4203985108" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">TUNING</text:a><text:s/>keyword in the input deck, if set to true.</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Note that only some of the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc146744_4203985108" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">TUNING</text:a> keyword parameters are processed.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A50&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="49">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">49</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-vtk-output</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Global switch for turning on writing VTK files. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A51&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="50">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">50</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-well-operability-check</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Enable the well operability checking. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A52&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="51">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">51</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-well-operability-check-iter</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Enable the well operability checking during iterations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A53&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="52">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">52</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--enable-write-all-solutions</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Write all solutions to disk instead of only the ones for the report steps. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A4" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A54&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="53">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">53</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.B2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--end-step</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.C2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Stop the simulation after this report step. A negative value runs to the end of the schedule. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">-1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A55&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="54">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">54</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--end-time</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The simulation time at which the simulation is finished [s]. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1e+100</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A56&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="55">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">55</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--explicit-rock-compaction</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Use pressure from end of the last time step when evaluating rock compaction. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A57&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="56">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">56</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--external-partition</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Name of file from which to load an externally generated partitioning of the model&apos;s active cells for MPI distribution purposes. If empty, the built-in partitioning method will be employed. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A58&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="57">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">57</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--force-disable-fluid-in-place-output</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Do not print fluid-in-place values after each report step even if requested by the deck.  Note this parameter will override the print request in the input deck.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A59&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="58">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">58</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--force-disable-resv-fluid-in-place-output</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Do not print reservoir volumes values after each report step even if requested by the deck.  Note this parameter will override the print request in the input deck.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A60&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="59">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">59</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--full-time-step-initially</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Always attempt to finish a report step using a single substep. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A61&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="60">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">60</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--gpu-aware-mpi</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. MPI communication use GPU aware MPI in the sense that it will use GPU direct communication. Setting this to true will require that the MPI implementation supports GPU direct communication. If you are unsure, set this to false. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A62&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="61">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">61</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--gpu-device-id</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Choose device ID for cusparseSolver or openclSolver, use &apos;nvidia-smi&apos; or &apos;clinfo&apos; to determine valid IDs. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A4" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A63&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="62">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">62</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.B2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--group-control-fraction-tolerance</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.C2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value. Tolerance for minimal allowed fraction for controlled phase before employing a fallback control. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.0001</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A64&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="63">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">63</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--hybrid-newton-config-file</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. JSON Config file path for Hybrid Newton. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;hybridNewtonConfig.json&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A65&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="64">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">64</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--ignore-keywords</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. List of Eclipse keywords which should be ignored. As a &apos;:&apos; separated string. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A66&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="65">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">65</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--ilu-fillin-level</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The fill-in level of the linear solver&apos;s ILU preconditioner. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A67&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="66">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">66</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--ilu-redblack</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Use red-black partitioning for the ILU preconditioner. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A68&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="67">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">67</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--ilu-relaxation</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value ranging from zero to one. The relaxation factor of the linear solver&apos;s ILU preconditioner. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.9</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A69&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="68">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">68</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--ilu-reorder-spheres</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Whether to reorder the entries of the matrix in the red-black ILU preconditioner in spheres starting at an edge. If false the original ordering is preserved in each color. Otherwise why try to ensure D4 ordering (in a 2D structured grid, the diagonal elements are consecutive). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A70&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="69">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">69</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--imbalance-tol</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Tolerable imbalance of the loadbalancing. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1.1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A71&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="70">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">70</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--initial-time-step-in-days</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The size of the initial time step in days. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A72&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="71">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">71</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--initial-time-step-size</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The size of the initial time step [s]. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">86400</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A73&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="72">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">72</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--inj-mult-damp-mult</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value ranging from zero to one. Injection multiplier dampening factor (dampening multiplied by this each time oscillation is detected). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.9</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A74&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="73">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">73</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--inj-mult-min-damp-factor</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value ranging from zero to one. Minimum injection multiplier dampening factor (maximum dampening level). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.05</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A75&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="74">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">74</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--inj-mult-osc-threshold</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Injection multiplier oscillation threshold (used for multiplier dampening). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A76&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="75">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">75</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--input-skip-mode</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A defined character string. Set compatibility mode for the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#REF_HEADING_KEYWORD_SKIP100_11_3" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">SKIP100</text:a> and <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#REF_HEADING_KEYWORD_SKIP300_11_3" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">SKIP300</text:a> keywords. Options are:</text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">100: skip <text:span text:style-name="NotKeyword">SKIP100</text:span>...ENDSKIP and keep <text:span text:style-name="NotKeyword">SKIP300</text:span>..ENDSKIP,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">300: skip <text:span text:style-name="NotKeyword">SKIP300</text:span>...ENDSKIP and keep <text:span text:style-name="NotKeyword">SKIP100</text:span>..ENDSKIP, or</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">all: skip both <text:span text:style-name="NotKeyword">SKIP100</text:span>...ENDSKIP and <text:span text:style-name="NotKeyword">SKIP300</text:span>...ENDSKIP.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;100&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A4" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A77&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="76">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">76</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--linear-solver</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A defined character string. Specify the configuration of the linear solver, valid values are:</text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">cprw<text:note text:id="ftn5" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>5</text:note-citation><text:note-body>
            <text:p text:style-name="Footnote">Wallis, J. R., Little, T. E., and Nolen, J. S.: &quot;Constrained Residual Acceleration of Conjugate Residual Methods,&quot; paper SPE 13536 presented at the SPE Reservoir Simulation Symposium, Dallas, Texas, USA (February 10-13, 1985).</text:p></text:note-body></text:note> <text:note text:id="ftn6" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>6</text:note-citation><text:note-body>
            <text:p text:style-name="Footnote">R. Scheichl, M. Roland, J. Wendebourg, Decoupling and block preconditioning for sedimentary basin simulations, Computational Geosciences 7 (2003) 295{318.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note><text:s/> <text:note text:id="ftn7" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>7</text:note-citation><text:note-body>
            <text:p text:style-name="Footnote">Klemetsdal, Ø.S., Møyner, O. &amp; Lie, KA. Accelerating multiscale simulation of complex geomodels by use of dynamically adapted basis functions. Comput Geosci 24, 459–476 (2020). https://doi.org/10.1007/s10596-019-9827-z.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note><text:s/>(default),</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">system_cpr (CPU-only), </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">system_cprw (CPU-only, system_cpr with the wells in the pressure stage), </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">ilu0, </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">dilu,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">cpr (an alias for cprw),</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">cpr_quasiimpes, </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">cpr_trueimpes, </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">cpr_trueimpesanalytic,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">amg<text:note text:id="ftn8" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>8</text:note-citation><text:note-body>
            <text:p text:style-name="Footnote">M. Blatt, A parallel algebraic multigrid method for elliptic problems with highly discontinuous coefficients, Ph.D. thesis, Ruprech<text:span text:style-name="T89">t-</text:span>Karls<text:span text:style-name="T89">-</text:span>Universit<text:span text:style-name="T85">ä</text:span>t Heidelberg (2010).</text:p></text:note-body></text:note>,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">hybrid (experimental), or </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">alternatively the name of a JSON file that contains the linear solver configuration parameters.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Option (1) extends the existing Constrained Pressure Residual (“CPR”) preconditioner to include wells. This option can also be invoked via the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc27871_3671211675" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">CPR</text:a> keyword in the <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc55591_1778172979" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">RUNSPEC</text:a> section; however, the command line parameter takes precedence.</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">For option (12) one enters a character string enclosed in quotes that defines the filename of a JSON configuration file for the flexible linear solver system. In this case the file extension should be ‘.json’. </text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Note that the Print (PRT) file contains the “Property tree for the linear solver” listing, which is the JSON specification of the current case, and can be used to configure a user specific linear solver JSON file.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;cprw&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A78&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="77">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">77</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--linear-solver-accelerator</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Choose the backend for the linear solver. Valid options are: cpu or gpu. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;cpu&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A79&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="78">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">78</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--linear-solver-ignore-convergence-failure</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Continue with the simulation like nothing happened after the linear solver did not converge.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A80&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="79">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">79</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--linear-solver-max-iter</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The maximum number of iterations of the linear solver. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">200</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A81&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="80">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">80</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--linear-solver-print-json-definition</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Write the JSON definition of the linear solver setup to the DBG file.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A82&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="81">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">81</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--linear-solver-reduction</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The minimum reduction of the residual which the linear solver must achieve. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.01</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A83&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="82">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">82</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--linear-solver-restart</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The number of iterations after which GMRES is restarted. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">40</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A84&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="83">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">83</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--linear-solver-verbosity</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Specify the output from the linear solver: </text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberOptions_3a_Table">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="0">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">No extra output,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">output per solution iteration, or</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">output per iteration.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A85&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="84">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">84</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--load-file</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. FileName for .OPMRST file used to load serialized state. If empty, CASENAME.OPMRST is used. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A86&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="85">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">85</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--load-step</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Specify if the simulator should load the serialized state from OPM Flow&apos;s version of the restart file, and should be set to either a specific report step, or 0 to load the last stored report step. </text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">The default value of -1 does not load the data from the OPM Flow specific restart file.</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">OPM Flow&apos;s version of the restart file, is written using the <text:span text:style-name="T61">--save-step=N</text:span> option.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">-1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A87&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="86">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">86</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--local-domains-ordering-measure</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Subdomain ordering measure. Allowed values are &apos;maxpressure&apos;, &apos;averagepressure&apos; and &apos;residual&apos;. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;maxpressure&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A88&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="87">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">87</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--local-domains-partition-well-neighbor-levels</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Number of neighbor levels around wells to include in the same domain during NLDD partitioning. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A89&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="88">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">88</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--local-domains-partitioning-imbalance</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value greater than one. Subdomain partitioning imbalance tolerance. 1.03 is 3 percent imbalance. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1.03</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A90&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="89">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">89</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--local-domains-partitioning-method</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Subdomain partitioning method. Allowed values are &apos;zoltan&apos;, &apos;simple&apos;, and the name of a partition file ending with &apos;.partition&apos;. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;zoltan&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A91&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="90">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">90</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--local-solve-approach</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Choose local solve approach. Valid choices are jacobi and gauss-seidel. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;gauss-seidel&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A92&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="91">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">91</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--local-tolerance-scaling-cnv</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Set lower than 1.0 to use stricter convergence tolerance for local solves. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A93&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="92">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">92</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--local-tolerance-scaling-mb</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Set lower than 1.0 to use stricter convergence tolerance for local solves. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A94&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="93">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">93</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--local-well-solve-control-switching</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Allow control switching during local well solutions. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A95&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="94">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">94</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--matrix-add-well-contributions</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Explicitly specify the influences of wells between cells in the Jacobian and preconditioner matrices. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A96&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="95">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">95</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-inner-iter-ms-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of inner iterations for multi-segment wells. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">100</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A97&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="96">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">96</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-inner-iter-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of inner iterations for standard wells. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">50</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A98&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="97">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">97</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-local-solve-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Max iterations for local solves with NLDD nonlinear solver. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">20</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A99&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="98">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">98</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-newton-iterations-with-inner-well-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum newton iterations with inner well iterations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">99</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A100&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="99">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">99</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-pressure-change-ms-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum relative pressure change for a single iteration of the multi-segment well model. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1e+06</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A101&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="100">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">100</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-residual-allowed</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Absolute maximum tolerated for residuals without cutting the time step size. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1e+07</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A102&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="101">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">101</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-single-precision-days</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum time step size where single precision floating point arithmetic can be used solving for the linear systems of equations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">20</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A103&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="102">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">102</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-temperature-change</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum absolute change of temperature in a single iteration. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">5</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A104&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="103">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">103</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-time-step-divisions</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The maximum number of divisions by two of the timestep size before the simulation bails out. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">10</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A105&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="104">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">104</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-time-step-size</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The maximum size to which all time steps are limited to [s]. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">inf</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A106&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="105">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">105</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-well-status-switch-for-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of status switching (stop&lt;-&gt;open) for a well during a time-step. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">99</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A107&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="106">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">106</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-well-status-switch-in-inner-iter-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of status switching (stop&lt;-&gt;open) for a well during inner iterations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">99</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A108&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="107">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">107</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--max-welleq-iter</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of iterations to determine solution the well equations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">30</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A109&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="108">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">108</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--maximum-number-of-group-switches</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of times a group can switch to the same control. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">3</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A110&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="109">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">109</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--maximum-number-of-well-switches</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of times a well can switch to the same control. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">3</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A111&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="110">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">110</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--maximum-water-saturation</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum water saturation. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A112&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="111">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">111</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--metis-params</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Configuration of Metis partitioner. You can request a configuration to be read from a JSON file by giving the filename here, with extension &apos;.json&apos;. See http://glaros.dtc.umn.edu/gkhome/fetch/sw/metis/manual.pdf for available METIS options. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;default&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A113&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="112">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">112</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--milu-variant</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A defined character string. Specify which variant of the modified ILU preconditioner ought to be used. Possible variants are: </text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">ilu: plain ILU (default),</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">milu_1: lump diagonal with dropped row entries,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">milu_2: lump diagonal with the sum of the absolute values of the dropped row entries,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">milu_3: if diagonal is positive add sum of dropped row entries. Otherwise subtract them,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">milu_4: if diagonal is positive add sum of dropped row entries. Otherwise do nothing.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;ilu&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A114&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="113">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">113</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--min-strict-cnv-iter</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Minimum number of Newton iterations before relaxed tolerances can be used for the CNV convergence criterion. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">-1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A115&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="114">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">114</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--min-strict-mb-iter</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Minimum number of Newton iterations before relaxed tolerances can be used for the MB convergence criterion. Default -1 means that the relaxed tolerance is used when maximum number of Newton iterations is reached. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">-1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A116&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="115">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">115</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--min-time-step-based-on-newton-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value greater than or equal to zero. The minimum time step size (in days for field and metric unit and hours for lab unit) can be reduced to based on newton iteration counts. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A117&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="116">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">116</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--min-time-step-before-shutting-problematic-wells-in-days</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value greater than or equal to zero. The minimum time step size in days for which problematic wells are not shut. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.01</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A118&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="117">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">117</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--min-time-step-size</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value greater than or equal to zero. The minimum size to which all time steps are limited to [s]. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A119&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="118">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">118</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--network-max-outer-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of outer iterations in the network solver before giving up. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">3</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A120&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="119">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">119</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--network-max-pressure-update-in-bars</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum pressure update in the inner network pressure update iterations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">5</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A121&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="120">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">120</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--network-max-strict-outer-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of outer iterations in network solver before relaxing tolerance. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">10</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A122&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="121">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">121</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--network-max-sub-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of sub-iterations to update network pressures (within a single well/group control update). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">100</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A123&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="122">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">122</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--network-pressure-update-damping-factor</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value ranging from zero to one. Damping factor in the inner network pressure update iterations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A124&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="123">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">123</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--newton-max-error</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The maximum error tolerated by the Newton method which does not cause an abort. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1e+100</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A125&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="124">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">124</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--newton-max-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The maximum number of Newton iterations per time step. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">20</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A126&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="125">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">125</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--newton-max-relax</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The maximum relaxation factor of a Newton iteration. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.5</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A127&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="126">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">126</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--newton-min-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The minimum number of Newton iterations per time step. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">2</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A128&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="127">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">127</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--newton-relaxation-type</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. The type of relaxation used by the Newton method. Valid options are: dampen or sor.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;dampen&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A129&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="128">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">128</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--newton-target-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The &apos;optimum&apos; number of Newton iterations per time step. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">10</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A130&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="129">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">129</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--newton-tolerance</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The maximum absolute error tolerated by the Newton method for considering a solution to be converged. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.01</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A131&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="130">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">130</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--newton-verbose</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Specify whether the Newton method should inform the user about its progress or not. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A132&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="131">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">131</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--newton-write-convergence</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Write the convergence behaviour of the Newton method to a VTK file. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A133&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="132">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">132</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--nldd-local-linear-solver</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Configuration of NLDD local linear solver. Valid options are: ilu0 (default), dilu, cpr_quasiimpes, and amg. Alternatively, you can request a configuration to be read from a JSON file by giving the filename here, ending with &apos;.json.&apos;. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;ilu0&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A134&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="133">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">133</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--nldd-local-linear-solver-max-iter</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The maximum number of iterations of the NLDD local linear solver. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">200</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A135&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="134">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">134</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--nldd-local-linear-solver-reduction</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The minimum reduction of the residual which the NLDD local linear solver must achieve. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.01</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A136&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="135">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">135</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--nldd-num-initial-newton-iter</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Number of initial global Newton iterations when running the NLDD nonlinear solver. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A4" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A137&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="136">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">136</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.B2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--nldd-num-overlap-layers</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.C2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Number of layers of overlap cells added around each NLDD subdomain. Overlap cells are solved for in the local problem, but are owned by another subdomain. Overlap is not extended across MPI ranks. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A138&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="137">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">137</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--nldd-relative-mobility-change-tol</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Threshold for single cell relative mobility change in the NLDD solver. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A139&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="138">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">138</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--nonlinear-solver</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Choose nonlinear solver. Valid choices are newton or nldd. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;newton&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A140&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="139">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">139</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--num-local-domains</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Number of local domains for NLDD nonlinear solver. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A141&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="140">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">140</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--num-overlap</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Numbers of layers overlap in parallel partition. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A142&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="141">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">141</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--num-pressure-points-equil</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Number of pressure points (in each direction) in tables used for equilibration. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">2000</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A143&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="142">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">142</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--num-satfunc-consistency-sample-points</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Maximum number of reported failures for each individual saturation function consistency check. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">5</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A144&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="143">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">143</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--nupcol-group-rate-tolerance</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Tolerance for acceptable changes in VREP/REIN group rates. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.001</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A145&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="144">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">144</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--opencl-ilu-parallel</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Parallelize ILU decomposition and application on GPU. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A146&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="145">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">145</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--opencl-platform-id</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Choose platform ID for openclSolver, use &apos;clinfo&apos; to determine valid platform IDs. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A147&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="146">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">146</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--output-dir</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. The directory to which result files are written. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A4" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A148&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="147">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">147</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--output-extra-convergence-info</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A defined character string. Specify whether to provide additional convergence output to separate files for diagnostic purposes. The available options are:</text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;none&quot; results in no extra output and overrides all other options.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;steps&quot; writes out convergence information per time step, to a CASENAME.INFOSTEP file. The file is useful for identifying numerical issues.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;iterations&quot; writes out non-linear convergence metrics, i.e., the MB and CNV values, per phase, for each non-linear iteration in each time step, to a CASENAME.INFOITER file.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;performance&quot; adds detailed timings to the performance summary at the end of the simulation.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Options can be combined with commas, e.g.&quot;steps,iterations&quot; for multiple outputs.</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">The default value of &quot;none&quot; prevents the two files from being written out, for better compatibility with the commercial simulator.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;none&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A149&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="148">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">148</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--output-interval</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Specify the number of report steps between two consecutive writes of restart data. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A150&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="149">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">149</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--output-mode</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A defined character string. Specify the output to the *.PRT and *.DBG files: </text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">“none”: No output to the files. </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">“log” or false: Output logging information only.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">“all” or true: Output everything.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">For example to just output logging information use:</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Example"><text:s text:c="4"/>--output-mode=“log”</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">or</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Example"><text:s text:c="4"/>--output-mode=false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;all&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A151&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="150">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">150</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--owner-cells-first</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Order cells owned by rank before ghost/overlap cells. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A152&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="151">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">151</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--parameter-file</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. An .ini file which contains a set of run-time parameters. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A153&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="152">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">152</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--parsing-strictness</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Set strictness of parsing process. Available options are:</text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;normal&quot;: stop for critical errors, and for unsupported keywords that would would change the simulator results if supported.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;high&quot;: stop for all errors, that is even for unsupported keywords that do not effect the results, for example <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc605466_3199477706" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">ECHO</text:a> and <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc605482_3199477706" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">NOECHO</text:a>.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;low&quot;: same as normal, except do not stop due to unsupported keywords that would change the simulator results if supported, and even if marked critical. </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;normal&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A154&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="153">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">153</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--partition-method</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Choose partitioning strategy:</text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;simple&quot;, </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;zoltan&quot;, </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;metis&quot;, </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;zoltanwell&quot; Zoltan with all cells perforated by a well represented by a single vertex. </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;zoltanwell&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A155&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="154">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">154</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--pre-solve-network</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Pre solve and iterate the network model at start-up. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A156&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="155">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">155</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--predetermined-time-steps-file</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. A file with a list of predetermined time step sizes (one time step per line). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A157&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="156">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">156</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--pressure-max</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum absolute pressure. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1e+99</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A158&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="157">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">157</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--pressure-min</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value. Minimum absolute pressure. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">-1e+99</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A159&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="158">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">158</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--pressure-scale</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Scaling of pressure primary variable. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A160&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="159">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">159</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--pri-var-oscilation-threshold</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The threshold value for the primary variable switching conditions after its meaning has switched to hinder oscillations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1e-05</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A161&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="160">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">160</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--print-parameters</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Specify the run time parameters to be printed at the start of the run: </text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberOptions_3a_Table">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="0">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">No output to the files. </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Output to *.DBG file.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Output to *.DBG and *.PRT files (default).</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">2</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A162&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="161">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">161</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--project-saturations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Option for doing saturation projection. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A4" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A163&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="162">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">162</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.B2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--rc-network-loose-coupling</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.C2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Reservoir coupling: exchange master/slave network pressures and rates only once per master outer network iteration (loose coupling) instead of the default once per inner sub-iteration (tight coupling). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A164&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="163">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">163</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--regularization-factor-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Regularization factor for wells. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">100</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A165&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="164">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">164</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--relaxed-linear-solver-reduction</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The minimum reduction of the residual which the linear solver need to achieve for the solution to be accepted. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.01</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A166&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="165">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">165</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--relaxed-max-pv-fraction</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The fraction of the pore volume of the reservoir where the volumetric error (CNV) may be violated during strict Newton iterations. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.03</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A167&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="166">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">166</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--relaxed-pressure-tol-msw</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Relaxed tolerance for the MSW pressure solution. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">10000</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A168&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="167">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">167</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--relaxed-well-flow-tol</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Relaxed tolerance for the well flow residual. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.001</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A5" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A169&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="168">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">168</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.B3" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--rescoup-spawn-wrapper</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.C3" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Developer flag for reservoir coupling, for debugging slave processes. If set, the master spawns this executable instead of the simulator for each slave rank, with the simulator path as the first argument followed by the slave's own arguments. The wrapper must start the simulator with exactly those arguments, for example with 'exec "$@"' in a shell script, or under a debugger for the rank to be debugged, and must keep running until the simulator exits. The slave name is in the --slave-log-file argument, the rank in the MPI runtime's environment (OMPI_COMM_WORLD_RANK for Open MPI). Has no effect in non-rescoup runs. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D3" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">""</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A5" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A170&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="169">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">169</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.B3" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--rescoup-sync-at-report-steps</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.C3" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Developer flag for reservoir coupling. If true, the master synchronizes with its slaves at slave report-step boundaries. If false (default), the master synchronizes at every master actual time step. Has no effect in non-rescoup runs. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D3" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A171&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="170">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">170</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--restart-time</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value. The simulation time at which a restart should be attempted [s]. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">-1e+35</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A172&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="171">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">171</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--restart-writing-interval</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The frequencies of which time steps are serialized to disk. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">16777215</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A173&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="172">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">172</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--save-file</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. FileName for .OPMRST file used for saving serialized state. If empty, CASENAME.OPMRST is used. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A174&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="173">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">173</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--save-step</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Specify if the simulator should save the serialized state of the OPM Flow simulator at one or more report steps to a special *.OPMRST file. This is in addition to the normal restart files written, and consumes significantly more space than the normal restart files, but restarting OPM Flow from this file using the <text:span text:style-name="T61">--load-step</text:span> option deviates less from the original run, compared to restarting using the normal restart features. The files produced are not compatible with other simulators, and also will not be compatible between different releases of OPM Flow.</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">The parameter should be set to one of the following:</text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;all&quot; to save all report steps,</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;last&quot; to save every step, keeping only the last.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;:x&quot; to save every x&apos;th step, or</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;x&quot; to save a specific time step.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Use negative values of &quot;x&quot; to keep only the last written step. </text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">The default value of &quot;&quot; does not write anything to the OPM Flow specific restart file.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A175&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="174">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">174</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--scale-linear-system</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Scale linear system according to equation scale and primary variable types. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A176&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="175">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">175</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--sched-restart</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Determine for a restart run if the case should initialize wells and groups from the historical <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc43945_784232322" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">SCHEDULE</text:a> section (true), or from the well and group data on the restart file (false).</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Note that the commercial simulator always uses data from the restart file (false).</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A177&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="176">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">176</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--serial-partitioning</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Perform partitioning for parallel runs on a single process. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A178&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="177">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">177</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--shut-unsolvable-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Shut unsolvable wells. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A179&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="178">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">178</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--slave</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Specify if the simulation is a slave simulation in a master-slave simulation.  Note that reservoir coupling is not currently supported. This is a developer option that should not be used.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A180&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="179">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">179</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--solve-welleq-initially</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Fully solve the well equations before each iteration of the reservoir model.  Note that the well equations are always added to the full system and solved until convergence.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">true</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A181&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="180">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">180</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--solver-continue-on-convergence-failure</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Continue instead of stop when minimum solver time step is reached. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A182&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="181">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">181</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--solver-growth-factor</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value greater than one. Specify the growth factor a time step can be increased by when recovering from one or more time step chops, subject to the maximum allowable time step size set by the <text:span text:style-name="T30">--solver-max-time-step-in-days</text:span> parameter. <text:s/></text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">For example, if the current time step has converged at 5 days after a time step chop, <text:s/>and --solver-growth-factor is set to the default value of 2.0, then the next time step will be 2.0 * 5 days, that is at 10 days.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">2</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A183&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="182">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">182</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--solver-max-growth</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value greater than one. Specify the maximum growth factor a time step can be increased by after a report time step, subject to the maximum allowable time step size set by the --solver-max-time-step-in-days parameter.</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Thus, if the current time step has converged at 5 days after at a report step, <text:s/>and --solver-max-growth is set to the default value of 3.0, then the next time step will be 3.0 * 5 days, that is at 15 days.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">3</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A184&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="183">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">183</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--solver-max-restarts</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The maximum number of breakdowns before a substep is given up and the simulator is terminated. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">10</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A185&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="184">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">184</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--solver-max-time-step-in-days</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The maximum size of a time step in days. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">365</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A186&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="185">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">185</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--solver-min-time-step</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The minimum size of a time step in days for field and metric and hours for lab. If a step cannot converge without getting cut below this step size the simulator will stop. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1e-12</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A187&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="186">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">186</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--solver-restart-factor</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value between zero and one. Specify the time step chop factor of the time step after a convergence failure. <text:s/></text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">For example, if the current non-convergent time step is 30 days and <text:span text:style-name="T22">--solver-restart-factor </text:span><text:s/>is set to the default value, then the time step will be repeated using 0.33 * 30 days as the time step, that is 9.9 days.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.33</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A188&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="187">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">187</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--solver-verbosity</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Specify the &quot;chattiness&quot; of the non-linear solver itself. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A189&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="188">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">188</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--strict-inner-iter-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Number of inner well iterations with strict tolerance. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">40</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A190&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="189">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">189</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--strict-outer-iter-wells</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Number of newton iterations for which wells are checked with strict tolerance. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">6</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A191&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="190">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">190</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--temperature-max</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Maximum absolute temperature. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1e+09</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A192&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="191">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">191</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--temperature-min</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value. Minimum absolute temperature. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A4" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A193&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="192">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">192</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--threads-per-process</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The maximum number of threads to be instantiated per process. If this parameter is not set then the default value 2 is used. If the parameter is &apos;-1&apos; then the number of threads will be determined by OpenMP, i.e., it will either be the environment variable OMP_NUM_THREADS or all available logical processors. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">2</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A194&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="193">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">193</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-after-event-in-days</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value. Specify the maximum allowed time step after an event; for example, when a well is open or closed etc. </text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">The default value of -1 means that events do not affect the time stepping.</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">-1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A195&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="194">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">194</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. The algorithm used to determine time-step sizes. Valid options are:</text:p>
       <text:list text:style-name="_40_NumberedListTable">
        <text:list-item text:start-value="1">
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&apos;pid&apos;: PID controller based adaptive time step control as suggested by Turek and Kuzmin<text:note text:id="ftn9" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>9</text:note-citation><text:note-body>
            <text:p text:style-name="Footnote">Algebraic Flux Correction III. Incompressible Flow Problems. Uni Dortmund, Turek and Kuzmin, January, 2006 (DOI: 10.1007/3-540-27206-2_8)</text:p></text:note-body></text:note>.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&apos;pid+iteration&apos;: Use PID and linear iteration numbers to guide the time step.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&apos;pid+newtoniteration&apos;: Use PID and non-linear iterations numbers to guide the time step.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&apos;iterationcount&apos;, </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&apos;newtoniterationcount&apos;, </text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&apos;general3rdorder&apos;: Use general 3rd order controller<text:note text:id="ftn99" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>99</text:note-citation><text:note-body>
            <text:p text:style-name="Footnote">Erik Hide Sæternes, Xing Cai, A control-theoretic approach to adaptive time stepping in reservoir simulations and its impacts on efficiency and robustness, Communications in Nonlinear Science and Numerical Simulation, Volume 158, 2026, 109828, ISSN 1007-5704, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cnsns.2026.109828.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note>, or</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&apos;hardcoded&apos;: Use time steps supplied by user via the time-step-control-file-name parameter.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;pid+newtoniteration&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A196&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="195">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">195</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-decay-damping-factor</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value less than or equal to one. The decay rate of the time step decrease when the target iterations is exceeded. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A197&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="196">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">196</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-decay-rate</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value less than one. The decay rate of the time step size of the number of target iterations is exceeded. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.75</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <text:soft-page-break/>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A198&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="197">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">197</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-file-name</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Specify the name of a file where time steps are specified.</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">For instance time steps can be generated by the summary application as per the following UNIX command line:</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Example">path_to_application/summary DECK <text:span text:style-name="NotKeyword">TIME</text:span> &gt; timesteps</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">Where:</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">DECK is the name of the data deck you want to get the time steps from,</text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents"><text:span text:style-name="NotKeyword">TIME</text:span> tells the application to return the timing for the run, and </text:p>
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">&quot;filename&quot; is the name of the file the times are piped to. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;timesteps&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A199&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="198">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">198</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-growth-damping-factor</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value greater than one. The growth rate of the time step increase when the target iterations is undercut. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">3.2</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A200&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="199">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">199</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-growth-rate</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A real value greater than one. The growth rate of the time step size of the number of target iterations is undercut. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1.25</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A201&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="200">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">200</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-max-reduction-time-step</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Only applicable for the general 3rd order controller, using &apos;control-error-filtering&apos; as time-step-control-tolerance-test-version. If the (proposed) relative change in time step size is larger than this parameter, the time step will be rejected. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A202&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="201">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">201</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-parameters</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Only applicable for the general 3rd order controller. Parameters for the general 3rd order controller. Should be given as &apos;beta_1;beta_2;beta_3;alpha_2;alpha_3&apos;. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;0.125;0.25;0.125;0.75;0.25&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A203&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="202">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">202</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-reject-completed-step</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A boolean value. Only applicable for the general 3rd order controller. Include rejection of completed time steps if the relative change is larger than the time step control tolerance. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">false</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A204&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="203">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">203</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-safety-factor</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value less than or equal to one. Value to be multiplied with the time step control tolerance to ensure that the target relative change is lower than the tolerance. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.8</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A205&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="204">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">204</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-target-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The number of linear iterations which the time step control scheme should aim for (if applicable). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">30</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A206&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="205">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">205</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-target-newton-iterations</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. The number of Newton iterations which the time step control scheme should aim for (if applicable). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">8</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A207&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="206">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">206</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-tolerance</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. The tolerance used by the time step size control algorithm. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A208&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="207">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">207</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-control-tolerance-test-version</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A character string. Only applicable for the general 3rd order controller. Ways to decide if the time step should be rejected. Options: &apos;standard&apos; and &apos;control-error-filtering&apos;. The standard version compares relative change to tolerance directly to decide if the time step should be rejected, while the control-error-filtering version compares the relative change in time step size to the max-reduction-time-step parameter. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">&quot;standard&quot;</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A209&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="208">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">208</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--time-step-verbosity</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">An integer value. Specify the &quot;chattiness&quot; during the time integration. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A210&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="209">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">209</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--tolerance-cnv</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Local convergence tolerance (maximum of local saturation errors). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.01</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A211&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="210">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">210</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--tolerance-cnv-energy</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Local energy convergence tolerance (maximum of local energy errors). </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">0.4182</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A212&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="211">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">211</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--tolerance-cnv-energy-relaxed</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Relaxed local energy convergence tolerance that applies for iterations after the iterations with the strict tolerance. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">41.82</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A213&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="212">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">212</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">--tolerance-cnv-relaxed</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents">A positive real value. Relaxed local convergence tolerance that applies for iterations after the iterations with the strict tolerance. </text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.D2" office:value-type="string">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">1</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
     </table:table-row>
     <table:table-row table:style-name="Table621.2">
      <table:table-cell table:style-name="Table621.A2" table:formula="ooow:&lt;A214&gt;+1" office:value-type="float" office:value="213">
       <text:p text:style-name="_40_Table_20_Contents_20_Center">213</text:p>
      </table:table-cell>
