        </draw:frame>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure14" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">2.15</text:sequence>: OPMRUN - Select Run Option Dialog</text:p>
      </draw:text-box>
     </draw:frame></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P74"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="P468"><text:span text:style-name="T6">The Run in No Simulation Mode option is equivalent to setting the </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc251745_4250154414" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T6">NOSIM</text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T6"> option in the input deck for all jobs in the queue (see </text:span>see section <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#5.2.32.NOSIM – Activates the No Simulation Mode for Data File Checking|outline" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="number-all-superior" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc27585_2267116897">Error: Reference source not found</text:bookmark-ref><text:s/><text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="text" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc27585_2267116897">Error: Reference source not found</text:bookmark-ref></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T6"><text:s/>and the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20">--enable-dry-run command line parameter in </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"><text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refTable0">Table 2.1</text:sequence-ref></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T20"><text:s/>in section </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#2.2.Running OPM Flow From The Command Line |outline" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T73">2.2 Running OPM Flow From The Command Line</text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T6">. This allows for checking all the jobs at once. </text:span></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P74">Selecting Run in Standard Simulation Mode will run all the jobs in the queue sequentially, with the OPM Flow terminal output directed to OPM Flow Output Element, as shown in <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refFigure15">Figure 2.16</text:sequence-ref>. The terminal output is also directed to a *.LOG file as well, similar to what the commercial simulator does. <text:s/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P74"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr16" draw:name="Frame25" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:y="0cm" svg:width="14.342cm" draw:z-index="25">
      <draw:text-box fo:min-height="9.155cm">
