          </office:binary-data>
         </draw:image>
        </draw:frame>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure20" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">2.21</text:sequence>: Corey Oil-Water Curves and Derivative Plot </text:p>
      </draw:text-box>
     </draw:frame>shows a typical Corey plot, with the plot at the top of the figure showing the Corey plot and the bottom plot showing the derivative plot, the data is also tabulated in <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refTable1">Table 2.2</text:sequence-ref>. Notice in <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refFigure20">Figure 2.21</text:sequence-ref><text:s/>that the water curve does not extend to 100% water saturation, this is an error as the water below the oil-water contact would have restrictive water flow.</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P451"/>
