    <text:p text:style-name="_40_Example"><text:s text:c="12"/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P518"><text:soft-page-break/>Amend the table as follows:</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552">-- <text:s text:c="69"/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552">-- <text:s text:c="6"/>WATER RELATIVE PERMEABILITY TABLES (SWFN) <text:s text:c="21"/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552">-- <text:s text:c="3"/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552">SWFN</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552">-- <text:s text:c="6"/>SWAT <text:s text:c="6"/>KRW <text:s text:c="7"/>PCOW <text:s text:c="36"/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552">-- <text:s text:c="6"/>FRAC <text:s text:c="6"/>FRAC <text:s text:c="6"/>PSIA <text:s text:c="36"/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552">-- <text:s text:c="6"/>-------- <text:s text:c="2"/>-------- <text:s text:c="2"/>------- <text:s text:c="33"/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552"><text:s text:c="10"/>0.30 <text:s text:c="5"/>0.0000 <text:s text:c="4"/>0.6190</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552"><text:s text:c="10"/><text:span text:style-name="T67">0.3</text:span>1<text:span text:style-name="T67"> <text:s text:c="5"/>0.0000 <text:s text:c="4"/></text:span>1*</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552"><text:s text:c="10"/>0.35 <text:s text:c="5"/>0.0005 <text:s text:c="4"/>0.3891</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552"><text:s text:c="10"/>0.40 <text:s text:c="5"/>0.0028 <text:s text:c="4"/>0.2279</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552"><text:s text:c="10"/>0.50 <text:s text:c="5"/>0.0237 <text:s text:c="4"/>0.0602</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552"><text:s text:c="10"/>0.60 <text:s text:c="5"/>0.0931 <text:s text:c="4"/>0.0077</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552"><text:s text:c="10"/>0.80 <text:s text:c="5"/>0.5000 <text:s text:c="4"/>0.0000</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P552"><text:s text:c="10"/>0.90 <text:s text:c="5"/>0.7000 <text:s text:c="4"/>0.0000</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P519"><text:s text:c="10"/>1.00 <text:s text:c="5"/>0.9000 <text:s text:c="4"/>0.0000 <text:s text:c="21"/>/ TABLE NO. 1</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P519"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="P518">The incorporation of the row for Sw equal to 0.31 should assist convergence and will not influence the oil in-place, although it will slightly reduce the water mobility between the water saturations of 0.30 and 0.31. Secondly, as one can see from <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refTable2">Table 2.3</text:sequence-ref><text:s/>the additional water saturation value did not cause any derivative discontinuities.</text:p>
