        </draw:frame><text:span text:style-name="T63"><text:line-break/></text:span>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure24" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">2.25</text:sequence>: Example Normalize Oil-Water Relative Permeability Curves</text:p>
      </draw:text-box>
     </draw:frame></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P602"><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P447">Notice how the distinction between <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc97395_621662414" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">KRO</text:a> and <text:a xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc70191_335817223">KRORW</text:a> is no longer present in the normalized curve in <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refFigure24">Figure 2.25</text:sequence-ref>, and similarly for <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc97397_621662414" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">KRW</text:a> and <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc70193_335817223" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">KRWR</text:a>, and <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc22881_7842323221" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">SWL</text:a> and <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc27248_784232322" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">SWCR</text:a>. Thus, the simulator will ignore one of each pair of end-points - this can lead to unexpected results for the de-normalized grid cell based saturation functions. An example is shown in <text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="category-and-value" text:ref-name="refFigure25">Figure 2.26</text:sequence-ref><text:s/>for a gas-water saturation table. Notice how the de-normalized end-point water relative permeability, <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc97397_621662414" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">KRW</text:a>, is only 0.20 versus 1.00 for the normalized value of <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#__RefHeading___Toc97397_621662414" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">KRW</text:a>. </text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P446"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr11" draw:name="Frame145" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="3.41cm" svg:y="-0.005cm" svg:width="11.227cm" draw:z-index="38">
