        </draw:frame>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure39" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">2.40</text:sequence>: Time Step Summary Showing Non-Convergence Example. </text:p>
      </draw:text-box>
     </draw:frame><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P554">Fortunately, OPM Flow has various controls that can resolve these type of issues similar to the commercial simulator, and in addition, and unlike the commercial simulator, OPM Flow has several linear solvers and preconditioners that increase the likelihood a solution may be found for various non-convergence issues.</text:p>
    <text:p text:style-name="P554"/>
    <text:p text:style-name="P554">As mentioned previously in section <text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="number-all-superior" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc643304_4138741440">Error: Reference source not found</text:bookmark-ref><text:s/><text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="text" text:ref-name="__RefHeading___Toc643304_4138741440">Error: Reference source not found</text:bookmark-ref>, convergence is <text:span text:style-name="T42">achieved</text:span> when <draw:frame draw:style-name="fr29" draw:name="Object502" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="1.042cm" svg:height="0.542cm" draw:z-index="97"><draw:object>
       <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
        <semantics>
         <mrow>
          <mi>R</mi>
          <mrow>
           <mo fence="true" form="prefix" stretchy="false">(</mo>
           <mrow>
            <msub>
             <mi>y</mi>
             <mi>n</mi>
            </msub>
           </mrow>
           <mo fence="true" form="postfix" stretchy="false">)</mo>
          </mrow>
         </mrow>
         <annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0">R(y_n)</annotation>
        </semantics>
       </math>
      </draw:object><draw:image>
